   "subject": "Re: plotting multiple QTL confidence intervals on plot of genetic map or with LOD curves",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Thank you! Sorry I forgot to mention that i am only trying to add CI to a LOD plot curve displaying only 3 LGs (and not all of them) with significant QTLs. The example you provided seems to add CI for a plot that has all of the chromosomes. In my case, I was wondering how I could modify the loop or script so that I can add CI only to  LG 6, 9,  and 12 in my study. I have already created a plot showing only those three LG, and the genome wide threshold. Thanks!"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CxWBsiWqwHwJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2014-09-29T13:17:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: plotting multiple QTL confidence intervals on plot of genetic map or with LOD curves",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">To plot selected chromosomes, use the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">chr</font> argument to <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">plot.scanone</font>, and also to <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">xaxisloc.scanone</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">. Here&#39;s an example. It&#39;s the same as before except the bits with </font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sigchr</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">.</font><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hyper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>hyper </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> calc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">genoprob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hyper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> step</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scanone</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hyper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>above3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> threshold</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sigchr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> above3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sigchr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">above3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    thischr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> above3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    ci </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lodint</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">thischr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    lo </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ci</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    hi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ci</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ci</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>    segments</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xaxisloc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scanone</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thischr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sigchr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>             xaxisloc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scanone</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thischr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sigchr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lwd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;violetred&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>    segments</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xaxisloc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"c